WEBVTT

00:00:03.010 --> 00:00:05.440
So these are the Lost Woods?

00:00:07.880 --> 00:00:08.860
It's kind of...

00:00:09.230 --> 00:00:11.570
dreary, wouldn't you say?

00:00:11.570 --> 00:00:14.620
Indeed. They're dark even in midday.

00:00:15.160 --> 00:00:18.480
What would you say to burning 
the entire place down?

00:00:18.480 --> 00:00:19.990
You know we can't do that!

00:00:20.280 --> 00:00:23.560
These woods are a fully inhabited ecosystem!

00:00:23.560 --> 00:00:25.080
I-I didn't seriously mean it.

00:00:25.400 --> 00:00:28.350
So it's deep within these woods, is it?

00:00:28.350 --> 00:00:29.050
Yeah.

00:00:29.050 --> 00:00:33.050
The Shield of Truth, 
which only the Hero can wield...

00:00:39.180 --> 00:00:48.860
<b>Beast Tamer</b>

00:02:06.480 --> 00:02:10.230
The Lost Woods

00:02:06.480 --> 00:02:10.230
The Lost Woods

00:02:09.400 --> 00:02:13.650
They say the Lost Woods 
are in a state of constant, rapid growth.

00:02:14.330 --> 00:02:18.870
I'll bet the map Arios's party made 
is totally worthless now.

00:02:19.710 --> 00:02:22.070
But we definitely have to 
find the item within?

00:02:22.430 --> 00:02:23.820
We definitely have to.

00:02:23.820 --> 00:02:25.790
That's our current job, after all.

00:02:26.870 --> 00:02:27.960
W...

00:02:28.300 --> 00:02:30.000
We're sorry.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:32.810
You call that an apology?

00:02:32.810 --> 00:02:34.130
You don't look sorry to me!

00:02:34.130 --> 00:02:36.220
I think you'd better try to sound 
a little more sincere!

00:02:36.220 --> 00:02:38.140
W-We're sorry!

00:02:38.140 --> 00:02:39.820
I still can't hear you!

00:02:39.820 --> 00:02:42.090
We're sorry!

00:02:42.090 --> 00:02:43.790
Should we forgive them?

00:02:43.790 --> 00:02:44.520
Yeah.

00:02:44.520 --> 00:02:46.300
I've gotten it out of my system.

00:02:46.300 --> 00:02:48.540
I'd say we can put this behind us.

00:02:48.540 --> 00:02:49.440
Agreed?

00:02:51.030 --> 00:02:52.760
Very well.

00:02:52.760 --> 00:02:54.970
I accept your request.

00:02:54.970 --> 00:02:56.950
Now, let's get to the issue.

00:02:57.450 --> 00:03:00.120
Apparently, the Shield of Truth 
is in the possession of monsters

00:03:00.120 --> 00:03:02.600
that dwell in the deepest depths 
of the Lost Woods.

00:03:02.600 --> 00:03:05.120
It's indispensable 
for defeating the Demon King.

00:03:05.450 --> 00:03:08.380
We must acquire it as swiftly as possible.

00:03:08.380 --> 00:03:10.710
For me, the Hero.

00:03:11.180 --> 00:03:13.580
The fate of the world is at stake.

00:03:13.580 --> 00:03:16.190
I don't see how you could possibly refuse.

00:03:16.190 --> 00:03:17.880
Is he attempting to order us around?

00:03:17.880 --> 00:03:19.980
I bet he's not really sorry!

00:03:20.670 --> 00:03:22.550
Hey, hold it, you two.

00:03:23.390 --> 00:03:25.580
Let's take the job.

00:03:29.690 --> 00:03:31.990
<i>I said we'd take the job, but...</i>

00:03:32.720 --> 00:03:36.380
Hey, are you really going to help that Hero?

00:03:36.380 --> 00:03:38.720
I don't like this one bit!

00:03:38.720 --> 00:03:40.150
I very much agree!

00:03:40.520 --> 00:03:45.120
I don't need those fools' help! 
I could defeat the Demon King all on my own!

00:03:45.680 --> 00:03:48.290
I'm not saying that 
because I'm worried about you, Rein!

00:03:48.290 --> 00:03:50.750
Rein, are you sure you're okay with this?

00:03:57.290 --> 00:03:59.950
Why did you just start rubbing our heads?!

00:03:59.950 --> 00:04:01.930
S-Sorry, I wasn't thinking!

00:04:01.930 --> 00:04:03.880
Th-That's okay...

00:04:03.880 --> 00:04:08.140
I was happy to see you guys 
get mad on my behalf.

00:04:09.190 --> 00:04:10.300
Rein...

00:04:10.300 --> 00:04:12.650
But I think we need to help Arios.

00:04:12.650 --> 00:04:15.100
He's the only one 
who can defeat the Demon King.

00:04:16.690 --> 00:04:19.340
Sorry to drag you along 
with this unpleasantness, though.

00:04:19.340 --> 00:04:21.370
I've come this far with you, after all.

00:04:21.370 --> 00:04:27.370
You're too kind for your own good, 
so it's my duty to look after you.

00:04:27.370 --> 00:04:28.680
Yeah, yeah!

00:04:28.680 --> 00:04:31.080
I like seeing you stay true to yourself!

00:04:31.500 --> 00:04:33.790
Thanks, Kanade, Tania.

00:04:35.840 --> 00:04:38.920
In that case, let's get in and out!

00:04:38.920 --> 00:04:41.020
But we need to first identify a strategy.

00:04:41.020 --> 00:04:42.890
We can't use the map, can we?

00:04:44.100 --> 00:04:47.680
I'd rather not just stumble 
our way around, either...

00:04:47.680 --> 00:04:49.720
Let's change our approach.

00:04:55.940 --> 00:04:59.040
I'll assimilate with a bird, like before.

00:04:59.040 --> 00:05:01.950
I can get the lay of the forest from above.

00:05:01.950 --> 00:05:04.990
You two look after my body 
and keep your eyes on our surroundings.

00:05:04.990 --> 00:05:06.030
Okay!

00:05:07.990 --> 00:05:10.320
Okay, be back soon!

00:05:10.700 --> 00:05:12.840
Take care!

00:05:12.840 --> 00:05:13.660
Sure!

00:05:17.580 --> 00:05:20.150
<i>It sure is a big forest...</i>

00:05:20.800 --> 00:05:24.760
<i>But although it's hidden, 
I can just make out a path.</i>

00:05:25.100 --> 00:05:27.990
<i>I should be able to find a route 
to its deepest point.</i>

00:05:35.760 --> 00:05:36.670
I'm back!

00:05:36.670 --> 00:05:38.230
Welcome back, Rein!

00:05:38.540 --> 00:05:40.490
Well? Did you find a path?

00:05:40.940 --> 00:05:42.150
Yeah, it went perfectly!

00:05:42.150 --> 00:05:43.930
Hooray!

00:05:43.930 --> 00:05:46.010
Then, let's get going!

00:05:46.010 --> 00:05:47.310
Wait, you!

00:05:47.310 --> 00:05:48.950
You don't know the way, Kanade!

00:05:49.310 --> 00:05:51.190
Oh, that's right!

00:05:56.620 --> 00:05:59.000
We've been walking for some time now...

00:05:59.000 --> 00:06:01.160
How much longer, Rein?

00:06:05.680 --> 00:06:06.720
That stone...

00:06:06.720 --> 00:06:09.820
We set it there to mark 
the way back, didn't we?

00:06:09.820 --> 00:06:11.430
Y-Yeah...

00:06:12.030 --> 00:06:13.630
We're back at square one.

00:06:13.630 --> 00:06:14.890
Seems so.

00:06:14.890 --> 00:06:17.600
Y-You think we picked the wrong path?

00:06:17.600 --> 00:06:19.480
That seems unlikely.

00:06:20.080 --> 00:06:23.560
I shared the information I gathered 
from above with the other birds.

00:06:24.020 --> 00:06:28.320
Even if I got it wrong, 
there's no way they all did.

00:06:28.320 --> 00:06:31.490
I think we followed the right path, as well.

00:06:31.490 --> 00:06:34.230
I think there's something more 
to these woods.

00:06:35.680 --> 00:06:37.750
Allow me to investigate, would you?

00:06:39.560 --> 00:06:41.160
Material Search.

00:06:45.250 --> 00:06:48.920
Wh... What are these lights?

00:06:48.920 --> 00:06:49.980
This way.

00:07:00.520 --> 00:07:01.750
I found it.

00:07:02.710 --> 00:07:06.200
This tree is emitting illusionary magic.

00:07:06.200 --> 00:07:07.900
That's the reason we lost our way.

00:07:08.640 --> 00:07:10.400
I-Illusionary magic?

00:07:10.400 --> 00:07:11.480
Yes.

00:07:11.480 --> 00:07:16.040
It establishes an expansive magical field 
that permeates the target's brain.

00:07:16.040 --> 00:07:19.770
Then by exposing the audiovisual processing 
center of the brain to its influence...

00:07:21.800 --> 00:07:22.750
In other words,

00:07:23.390 --> 00:07:29.880
a spell has been cast on us that prevents us 
from doing anything but walking in circles.

00:07:29.880 --> 00:07:33.510
Though the scale of it suggests 
it's more of a barrier than a spell.

00:07:34.160 --> 00:07:35.850
I see...

00:07:36.200 --> 00:07:39.390
Now then, Kanade. 
Break down this tree, would you?

00:07:39.390 --> 00:07:40.300
How come?

00:07:40.300 --> 00:07:41.630
Venting frustrations?

00:07:41.630 --> 00:07:42.570
Certainly not!

00:07:42.570 --> 00:07:44.440
Just who do you think I am?!

00:07:44.440 --> 00:07:45.940
Please don't fight!

00:07:46.720 --> 00:07:49.310
The tree is projecting the barrier.

00:07:49.310 --> 00:07:51.950
Eliminating it should allow us 
to make progress.

00:07:51.950 --> 00:07:53.040
Oh, got it!

00:07:53.040 --> 00:07:54.160
Er, Tania...

00:07:54.160 --> 00:07:54.780
Yes?

00:07:55.210 --> 00:07:58.010
Can't you just take down the barrier?

00:07:58.010 --> 00:07:59.200
Without destroying the tree...

00:08:00.340 --> 00:08:02.160
It's quite powerful.

00:08:02.560 --> 00:08:05.690
I could do it, but it may take a long time.

00:08:05.690 --> 00:08:06.970
I see.

00:08:06.970 --> 00:08:10.080
If we're too late, 
that Hero will make fun of Rein!

00:08:10.080 --> 00:08:11.320
I won't let it happen!

00:08:11.320 --> 00:08:12.880
Rein, let me do it!

00:08:12.880 --> 00:08:13.630
Wait, Kanade—

00:08:15.490 --> 00:08:17.140
Leave this place.

00:08:17.140 --> 00:08:19.720
Wh-What was that voice?!

00:08:19.720 --> 00:08:23.310
Leave this place. Leave this place.

00:08:23.310 --> 00:08:25.040
Leave this place.

00:08:25.040 --> 00:08:26.600
Leave this place.

00:08:27.520 --> 00:08:29.360
Leave this place.

00:08:29.790 --> 00:08:30.820
It can't be...

00:08:39.210 --> 00:08:40.660
A fairy.

00:08:41.000 --> 00:08:43.910
<i>One of the ultimate species 
like Kanade and Tania.</i>

00:08:44.520 --> 00:08:47.630
<i>Spellcasting specialists with magic power 
even greater than dragonoids!</i>

00:08:47.930 --> 00:08:52.600
<i>But humans haven't seen a fairy 
in two hundred years.</i>

00:08:53.400 --> 00:08:56.810
<i>As denizens of the mountains and forests,</i>

00:08:56.810 --> 00:09:00.580
<i>they viewed humans, who harvested the forests 
for resources, as their mortal enemies.</i>

00:09:01.250 --> 00:09:04.270
<i>Soon, conflict sprang up 
between the two groups,</i>

00:09:04.270 --> 00:09:08.360
<i>and the fairies retreated to the hinterlands 
where humans couldn't reach them.</i>

00:09:09.160 --> 00:09:14.030
<i>Because of that, fairies hold humans 
in a great deal of contempt.</i>

00:09:14.480 --> 00:09:15.570
U-Um...

00:09:16.030 --> 00:09:16.780
Hello—

00:09:16.780 --> 00:09:17.740
Leave this place.

00:09:17.740 --> 00:09:20.330
Um... I was hoping to talk—

00:09:20.330 --> 00:09:21.410
Leave this place.

00:09:21.410 --> 00:09:24.460
I'm Rein. These are my comrades...

00:09:24.460 --> 00:09:25.960
Leave this place.

00:09:25.960 --> 00:09:28.360
There's actually something 
we have to do in this—

00:09:28.360 --> 00:09:29.520
Leave this place.

00:09:29.520 --> 00:09:31.420
If you won't leave this place...

00:09:32.000 --> 00:09:34.130
I'll remove you from it.

00:09:34.130 --> 00:09:35.560
W-We'll come back later!

00:09:35.560 --> 00:09:36.840
Very well!

00:09:41.480 --> 00:09:43.530
Sh-She didn't pursue us?

00:09:43.530 --> 00:09:45.100
No, I think we're safe.

00:09:45.940 --> 00:09:48.080
What a shock!

00:09:48.080 --> 00:09:49.450
What in the world was that?

00:09:49.450 --> 00:09:51.950
Just threatening us 
out of the blue like that...

00:09:51.950 --> 00:09:55.950
Aren't fairies supposed to be 
a warm and welcoming species?

00:09:55.950 --> 00:09:56.570
Yeah...

00:09:57.150 --> 00:10:00.200
It's unusual that she even 
showed herself like that.

00:10:00.200 --> 00:10:02.480
It would be one thing 
if it were just the two of you,

00:10:02.480 --> 00:10:04.160
but with a human like me there?

00:10:04.160 --> 00:10:06.540
She'd never usually show herself.

00:10:06.540 --> 00:10:08.730
Are you suggesting 
there's something more at play?

00:10:08.730 --> 00:10:09.500
Yeah.

00:10:09.500 --> 00:10:13.150
I think it's because we got 
close to the barrier.

00:10:13.150 --> 00:10:16.210
Indeed, she revealed herself 
when Kanade tried to break it...

00:10:16.210 --> 00:10:20.080
Because you said it was 
the only way to move on!

00:10:20.080 --> 00:10:21.190
Huh?

00:10:21.190 --> 00:10:26.380
Didn't you say there's a monster 
with the Shield of Truth inside that barrier?

00:10:26.380 --> 00:10:30.330
But when I tried to break the barrier, 
that girl came out and...

00:10:30.330 --> 00:10:31.560
It does seem strange.

00:10:32.040 --> 00:10:36.010
Would she really cooperate with monsters 
out of sheer hatred of humans?

00:10:36.010 --> 00:10:38.830
Well, her motives aside...

00:10:38.830 --> 00:10:40.750
We're in quite a hurry, aren't we?

00:10:40.750 --> 00:10:43.540
I believe we should take down 
the barrier and proceed.

00:10:44.260 --> 00:10:46.490
She caught us by surprise before,

00:10:46.490 --> 00:10:48.800
but I can keep her spellcasting at bay.

00:10:48.800 --> 00:10:51.840
While I do, Kanade, you destroy the tree.

00:10:51.840 --> 00:10:53.050
I see!

00:10:53.050 --> 00:10:55.160
Then we won't actually harm her.

00:10:55.160 --> 00:10:56.250
You can agree to that, can't you?

00:11:00.130 --> 00:11:03.140
Well... I'd really rather 
talk to her one more time.

00:11:04.640 --> 00:11:05.630
You can't!

00:11:05.630 --> 00:11:08.400
She clearly had no interest in talking!

00:11:08.400 --> 00:11:11.470
Yeah! It's not safe!

00:11:11.470 --> 00:11:13.690
I'd rather avoid use of force if possible...

00:11:14.430 --> 00:11:18.990
Besides, we were kind of defensive 
back there ourselves, weren't we?

00:11:18.990 --> 00:11:22.700
If we approach without hostility, 
I think we can work it all out.

00:11:24.400 --> 00:11:25.560
Rein is just...

00:11:25.560 --> 00:11:26.750
Truly...

00:11:26.750 --> 00:11:29.130
...too kind for his own good!

00:11:44.180 --> 00:11:45.640
Leave this place.

00:11:45.640 --> 00:11:47.800
We're not your enemies.

00:11:47.800 --> 00:11:49.450
We want to talk to you.

00:11:50.270 --> 00:11:51.810
Leave this place.

00:11:51.810 --> 00:11:54.590
We aren't here to disrupt the forest.

00:11:54.590 --> 00:11:56.520
We just have business inside!

00:11:56.910 --> 00:11:58.780
If you won't leave this place...

00:11:58.780 --> 00:12:00.660
Go on and attack me if you want.

00:12:01.240 --> 00:12:04.190
If that will build trust between us, 
I'll accept that.

00:12:04.190 --> 00:12:07.120
But please don't hurt these two behind me.

00:12:07.120 --> 00:12:08.270
Hey, wait!

00:12:08.270 --> 00:12:10.960
Really? In that case...

00:12:10.960 --> 00:12:12.540
I will purge you now.

00:12:15.000 --> 00:12:15.880
Rein!

00:12:15.880 --> 00:12:17.050
<i>It's okay.</i>

00:12:17.050 --> 00:12:18.840
<i>I can endure one attack.</i>

00:12:19.320 --> 00:12:21.090
<i>But I won't give up, no matter what.</i>

00:12:22.160 --> 00:12:24.130
<i>I'm a beast tamer.</i>

00:12:24.570 --> 00:12:28.250
<i>I've been through countless situations 
where I couldn't communicate with words.</i>

00:12:28.680 --> 00:12:29.900
<i>And yet...</i>

00:12:30.680 --> 00:12:33.890
<i>If you engage in good faith, 
your feelings <i>will</i> get through.</i>

00:12:35.330 --> 00:12:36.700
<i>I know that.</i>

00:12:38.720 --> 00:12:40.570
Illusion Arrow!

00:12:45.240 --> 00:12:47.150
Why won't you run away?

00:12:47.150 --> 00:12:47.990
Don't you remember?

00:12:48.270 --> 00:12:50.200
All I want to do is talk!

00:12:50.610 --> 00:12:54.920
You let my attack hit you, 
merely to earn my trust?

00:12:56.840 --> 00:12:58.380
I do not understand.

00:12:58.800 --> 00:13:01.110
Are you truly human?

00:13:01.530 --> 00:13:07.760
Like those who stole, defiled, 
and trampled on our lands?

00:13:08.610 --> 00:13:09.950
I am.

00:13:09.950 --> 00:13:12.170
But we're not all like that.

00:13:12.720 --> 00:13:15.230
There are plenty of good humans out there.

00:13:16.180 --> 00:13:18.700
I can't promise you that I'm one of them,

00:13:18.700 --> 00:13:20.220
but I do hope you'll trust me.

00:13:20.220 --> 00:13:22.250
I... I...

00:13:24.120 --> 00:13:25.650
I shall not be deceived!

00:13:31.330 --> 00:13:33.660
You two... Why?!

00:13:33.660 --> 00:13:35.160
We couldn't just stand back and watch!

00:13:35.160 --> 00:13:37.870
Even if you told us to leave it to you, 
we were still worried!

00:13:38.200 --> 00:13:39.920
Yes, you went too far.

00:13:39.920 --> 00:13:41.960
You clearly weren't getting through!

00:13:42.680 --> 00:13:44.100
Listen to me!

00:13:44.670 --> 00:13:48.120
Rein really isn't a bad person!

00:13:48.120 --> 00:13:51.160
He saved me when I was in trouble.

00:13:51.160 --> 00:13:55.400
And he helped the people 
in the city, and, um...

00:13:55.400 --> 00:13:59.050
Precisely! I, as a dragonoid, 
vouch for him, as well.

00:13:59.050 --> 00:14:03.280
Remember? Rein was against 
destroying the forest from the start!

00:14:03.640 --> 00:14:04.890
Yeah!

00:14:04.890 --> 00:14:07.950
When Tania wanted to burn 
the place down, he got really mad!

00:14:07.950 --> 00:14:09.630
I-I wasn't serious about that!

00:14:09.630 --> 00:14:13.120
But when you attempted to destroy 
the tree, Rein stopped you!

00:14:13.520 --> 00:14:16.350
You're the one who told me to!

00:14:16.350 --> 00:14:18.710
But you still <i>wanted</i> to do it, correct?

00:14:19.000 --> 00:14:21.800
But it was still your idea!

00:14:20.000 --> 00:14:22.760
This is no time to fight, you two!

00:14:21.950 --> 00:14:23.420
What a curious human.

00:14:24.040 --> 00:14:27.380
A curious cat spirit and dragonoid, as well...

00:14:30.640 --> 00:14:35.430
Never before have I met 
creatures like yourselves.

00:14:36.500 --> 00:14:37.660
What is your name?

00:14:38.100 --> 00:14:40.000
Rein Shroud.

00:14:40.000 --> 00:14:41.400
I am Sora.

00:14:42.280 --> 00:14:44.870
I will hear what you have to say.

00:14:47.320 --> 00:14:49.000
I see.

00:14:49.000 --> 00:14:54.110
You seek the Shield of Truth 
in that Hero's stead.

00:14:54.110 --> 00:14:55.770
Is this correct?

00:14:55.770 --> 00:14:56.880
Yeah.

00:14:56.880 --> 00:14:58.790
But the barrier's holding us back.

00:14:59.180 --> 00:15:01.500
It was I who erected the barrier.

00:15:01.880 --> 00:15:04.200
Would you be willing 
to take it down to let us—

00:15:04.200 --> 00:15:05.590
I cannot.

00:15:06.030 --> 00:15:10.940
The barrier severs the path 
to the fairies' village.

00:15:10.940 --> 00:15:13.430
I must not expose my comrades to danger.

00:15:13.430 --> 00:15:16.920
It sounds to me like you're 
covering for a monster.

00:15:16.920 --> 00:15:17.920
I am not.

00:15:17.920 --> 00:15:22.150
There is no monster in this forest 
which holds the Shield of Truth.

00:15:22.670 --> 00:15:26.460
All that exists in its depths 
is the path to the fairies' village.

00:15:26.460 --> 00:15:29.740
It is the fairies who protect 
the Shield of Truth.

00:15:29.740 --> 00:15:31.200
Really?!

00:15:31.600 --> 00:15:33.980
Huh? But what about the monster?

00:15:33.980 --> 00:15:37.410
I'm sure someone fed bad intelligence 
to that ridiculous Hero.

00:15:39.220 --> 00:15:42.490
If it is necessary to vanquish 
the Demon King, I shall give it to you.

00:15:42.490 --> 00:15:44.000
Allow me a moment.

00:15:52.080 --> 00:15:53.260
Take it.

00:15:53.260 --> 00:15:55.260
A-Are you sure about this?

00:15:55.260 --> 00:15:56.200
I am.

00:15:56.200 --> 00:15:58.040
Though I may despise humans,

00:15:58.040 --> 00:16:00.700
my hatred for monsters runs deeper.

00:16:02.260 --> 00:16:05.510
<i>Th-That seemed a little too easy...</i>

00:16:06.290 --> 00:16:07.440
We did it, though!

00:16:07.440 --> 00:16:10.220
Is there anything I can do to thank you?

00:16:10.220 --> 00:16:11.900
No need, I'm sure.

00:16:12.440 --> 00:16:14.480
To pass along the Shield of Truth

00:16:14.480 --> 00:16:19.640
was an ancient pact made between 
the fairies and the previous Hero.

00:16:19.640 --> 00:16:21.870
I merely upheld that pact.

00:16:21.870 --> 00:16:23.120
R-Really?

00:16:23.120 --> 00:16:25.100
Yes. I deserve no gratitude.

00:16:25.100 --> 00:16:27.960
She says you don't need to thank her, 
so I'm sure it's fine!

00:16:28.300 --> 00:16:30.590
Well, that's one job complete!

00:16:30.590 --> 00:16:33.240
Let's get back to the city and hand it over!

00:16:33.240 --> 00:16:35.610
Y-Yeah, sure thing.

00:16:35.610 --> 00:16:37.160
Thanks, Sora.

00:16:37.160 --> 00:16:39.760
Now that your business is done, 
leave this place.

00:16:39.760 --> 00:16:41.220
R-Right...

00:16:42.100 --> 00:16:43.530
Rein, Rein!

00:16:43.530 --> 00:16:45.800
Can I have a better look at that shield?

00:16:45.800 --> 00:16:46.520
Sure thing!

00:16:46.520 --> 00:16:48.080
Just don't break it.

00:16:48.080 --> 00:16:49.570
I won't!

00:16:54.170 --> 00:16:55.370
What's the matter?

00:16:55.960 --> 00:16:57.280
Hey, Sora...

00:16:57.280 --> 00:16:59.440
There's something bothering you, isn't there?

00:17:01.200 --> 00:17:05.040
I can't say why. It's just a feeling I got.

00:17:05.040 --> 00:17:07.540
Even if it's a small thing, 
I'm happy to listen.

00:17:08.080 --> 00:17:11.250
And you did fetch us 
the Shield of Truth, so...

00:17:11.530 --> 00:17:14.730
there's a chance I could help you.

00:17:17.040 --> 00:17:19.000
Well... the truth is...

00:17:19.000 --> 00:17:21.480
I... I...

00:17:22.950 --> 00:17:24.990
<i>No, I must not reveal it.</i>

00:17:24.990 --> 00:17:26.510
<i>If I reveal the truth...</i>

00:17:27.150 --> 00:17:29.650
<i>he'll likely aid me...</i>

00:17:30.650 --> 00:17:33.180
<i>and they could all be hurt.</i>

00:17:33.900 --> 00:17:36.570
No... it's nothing.

00:17:36.570 --> 00:17:37.550
I don't mind.

00:17:38.320 --> 00:17:40.670
Even if it's dangerous, I don't mind.

00:17:40.670 --> 00:17:42.760
If you're in trouble, I want to help.

00:17:43.390 --> 00:17:45.020
Won't you let me?

00:17:45.430 --> 00:17:46.650
B-But...

00:17:46.650 --> 00:17:48.150
That's just the kind of guy he is.

00:17:48.500 --> 00:17:51.240
He's so excessively kind 
that it's frankly disgusting.

00:17:51.240 --> 00:17:53.450
He simply won't accept "no" for an answer.

00:17:53.450 --> 00:17:56.800
Well? Why not give us a chance?

00:17:56.800 --> 00:17:57.630
Wh—

00:17:57.630 --> 00:18:01.260
I think you should do it, too!

00:18:01.260 --> 00:18:03.120
Don't worry!

00:18:03.120 --> 00:18:05.930
We're a lot stronger than we look!

00:18:06.600 --> 00:18:09.650
I really think we could help you!

00:18:13.350 --> 00:18:14.570
Then...

00:18:14.570 --> 00:18:19.030
having deemed you worthy 
of my trust, I shall reveal all.

00:18:20.070 --> 00:18:22.240
I have a younger twin sister.

00:18:23.140 --> 00:18:25.100
Her name is Runa.

00:18:25.100 --> 00:18:29.580
Her personality is the opposite of mine, 
yet we remain close.

00:18:31.700 --> 00:18:34.010
She is precious to me.

00:18:35.300 --> 00:18:39.840
In truth, there is more than one path 
to the fairies' village.

00:18:39.840 --> 00:18:42.460
There are many, found all over the world.

00:18:42.940 --> 00:18:48.150
Together, Runa and I maintained 
the barrier within the Lost Woods.

00:18:49.110 --> 00:18:51.860
It was, in truth, dull work.

00:18:54.840 --> 00:18:59.610
But in Runa's company, 
there was much joy to be found.

00:19:00.360 --> 00:19:01.320
But...

00:19:01.860 --> 00:19:07.370
That day, we were obliged to leave 
the barrier for a time, for certain reasons.

00:19:07.870 --> 00:19:08.780
And there...

00:19:10.120 --> 00:19:13.630
we encountered a monster 
working for the Demon King's army.

00:19:14.210 --> 00:19:16.360
We swiftly attempted 
to return from whence we came,

00:19:16.360 --> 00:19:19.300
but it pursued, and we were 
forced to fight back.

00:19:21.870 --> 00:19:24.300
However, we failed to defeat it.

00:19:25.050 --> 00:19:25.850
And then...

00:19:31.760 --> 00:19:34.020
Runa was captured.

00:19:34.020 --> 00:19:36.620
A monster even fairies couldn't beat?

00:19:36.620 --> 00:19:39.500
The monster's name was Shadow Knight.

00:19:39.500 --> 00:19:42.080
I see... that explains it.

00:19:42.080 --> 00:19:43.490
Wh-What do you mean?

00:19:44.160 --> 00:19:46.590
A Shadow Knight is a C-rank monster,

00:19:46.590 --> 00:19:49.520
so it shouldn't be able 
to beat an ultimate species.

00:19:49.520 --> 00:19:51.990
But it does have one tricky characteristic.

00:19:52.670 --> 00:19:55.840
It nullifies all magic attacks.

00:19:55.840 --> 00:19:59.550
In other words, only physical attacks 
can hurt a Shadow Knight.

00:19:59.550 --> 00:20:03.070
Meanwhile, fairies specialize 
exclusively in magic.

00:20:03.070 --> 00:20:05.010
It was a bad match-up for them.

00:20:05.370 --> 00:20:09.210
I was wondering what could 
possibly beat two fairies.

00:20:09.720 --> 00:20:11.030
That does explain it.

00:20:11.030 --> 00:20:11.730
Yes.

00:20:12.280 --> 00:20:16.190
The Shadow Knight's aim was to eliminate 
the ultimate species that might oppose them.

00:20:16.930 --> 00:20:21.400
It ordered me to lower the barrier 
in exchange for Runa's release.

00:20:21.400 --> 00:20:26.620
But I refused to place 
my other comrades in danger.

00:20:27.300 --> 00:20:31.830
Powerless to save her alone, 
I entreated our village's leader for aid.

00:20:32.530 --> 00:20:36.130
But he encouraged me, instead, 
to abandon her.

00:20:37.040 --> 00:20:40.810
"We must celebrate the fact that 
the others are safely within the barrier."

00:20:40.810 --> 00:20:43.560
"It was you two who erred 
by leaving the barrier's safety."

00:20:43.560 --> 00:20:46.750
"You must accept 
the consequences of your actions."

00:20:47.600 --> 00:20:49.070
That's awful...

00:20:49.070 --> 00:20:50.180
Unacceptable!

00:20:50.600 --> 00:20:52.680
I understand our leader's reasoning.

00:20:53.140 --> 00:20:59.110
He prioritizes the lives 
of all fairies over that of my sister.

00:20:59.880 --> 00:21:03.320
I understand that... and yet...

00:21:03.800 --> 00:21:05.070
And yet I...

00:21:05.880 --> 00:21:10.630
I am unable to simply abandon my sister.

00:21:17.160 --> 00:21:19.250
You've been working so hard.

00:21:19.860 --> 00:21:22.780
You've been enduring all that pain alone.

00:21:23.300 --> 00:21:25.220
But you can rest easy now.

00:21:25.610 --> 00:21:26.910
I make you this promise.

00:21:26.910 --> 00:21:28.780
We will save your sister.

00:21:29.680 --> 00:21:32.300
We won't expose your people to danger.

00:21:32.960 --> 00:21:35.140
And we will defeat the Shadow Knight.

00:21:35.140 --> 00:21:36.140
All of it.

00:21:36.790 --> 00:21:40.030
We'll grant all of it, together.

00:23:35.560 --> 00:23:39.980
The Captive Fairy

00:23:36.440 --> 00:23:39.420
Next Time: "The Captive Fairy."
